      "type": "about",
      "tabLabel": "About",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Steal War",
          "subtitle": "War",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "War variant where players can steal cards from opponents. More strategic than classic War."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Reported by Gary Philippy and Hayes Ruberti; hybrid of War and Stealing Bundles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Two players. Each has a face-down packet of 27 cards (half the deck); no hand is held. Both look at the top card before playing and may use it to battle or to steal the opponent's face-up capture pile if the rank matches."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "52 cards plus 2 jokers"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Cards or tiles"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal out all cards evenly so each player has 27 cards in a face-down packet."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Variations",
          "subtitle": "Known ways this game changes",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "style": "unordered",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Protection rule: Playing a card that matches your own pile top protects that pile from being stolen during that turn (resolves timing when both players could steal)."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
